## 2. CLAUDE.md files

Claude Code loads the root `CLAUDE.md` plus the nearest `CLAUDE.md` above whatever file is being touched — so a change under `backend/src/controllers/` picks up root + `backend/CLAUDE.md` automatically, with no glob configuration needed (unlike the Cursor `.mdc` files, which had to declare `globs:`/`alwaysApply:` per rule). Each file below is intentionally short: it points at the docs that carry the actual rules rather than restating them, plus the couple of process instructions that are genuinely new to this repo.

**`.claude/CLAUDE.md`** (root — always loaded):
```md
# Aaradhya Event Management — Root Rules

Read before any change:
@docs/coding-guidelines.md
@docs/naming-conventions.md
@docs/git-guidelines.md
@docs/directory-structure.md

## Spec is the source of truth
- Full spec: docs/spec/Aaradhya_SRS_v1.1.md
- Work is sliced into stories: docs/stories/Aaradhya_Story_Backlog.md
- Never implement beyond what the current story's Acceptance Criteria asks for.
  If the spec and the story conflict, or the story is ambiguous, stop and ask —
  don't guess and don't silently expand scope.

## Every change is scoped to one story
- State the STORY-ID you're implementing at the start of the session.
- Commits and PR titles reference it — see docs/git-guidelines.md and the
  workflow in docs/dev-process.md for the exact format.
```

**`backend/CLAUDE.md`**:
```md
# Aaradhya Backend Rules

Inherits the root rules. Backend-specific:
@docs/handler-patterns.md
@../docs/api-conventions.md

## Layering
- routes/ wires HTTP method + path to a controller. No logic here.
- controllers/ is the handler — owns the DB call and the business logic
  (see handler-patterns.md — read "resolver" as "route handler").
- services/ holds pure, DB-free computation (totals, rollups, overlap
  queries) so it's unit-testable without a running server or DB.
- Only extract to utils/ once a pattern genuinely repeats — don't
  pre-abstract for a single caller.

## Every derived/computed field is server-computed, never client-trusted
Per the SRS: accommodation totals, payment balance, item total_cost, and
the quotation rollup are always recalculated server-side; a client-submitted
value for any of them is ignored, not validated-and-accepted.
```

**`frontend/CLAUDE.md`**:
```md
# Aaradhya Frontend Rules

Inherits the root rules. Frontend-specific:
@docs/react-guidelines.md
@docs/style-guide.md
@../docs/design/theme-tokens.md

## Before building a component
Check components/ui/ first — do not build a new common control that
