## 3. The `review-standards` skill

Merge Voyager's `fe-review` and `api-review` skills — they're already identical apart from the name, and neither actually contains GraphQL-specific logic (they just point at whatever `docs/` holds). One skill, callable from either `backend/` or `frontend/` context:

`.claude/skills/review-standards/SKILL.md` — same process as the source: pin a fixed point (`git diff <ref>...HEAD`), read whatever `docs/*.md` and the nearest `CLAUDE.md` document, check the diff against them, and layer the Fowler smell baseline (Mysterious Name, Duplicated Code, Feature Envy, Data Clumps, Primitive Obsession, Repeated Switches, Shotgun Surgery, Divergent Change, Speculative Generality, Message Chains, Middle Man, Refused Bequest) as judgement calls under whatever the repo docs already settle. No content change needed beyond removing the "GraphQL/AppSync" framing from the skill's own description line, since it never actually depended on that stack. Invoke it as the standards gate between "test" and "commit" in the workflow below.

